WEBVTT

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.960
Hey! I'm Pinky.

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:07.160
Today I'm going to save you from doing extra work on algebra

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.035
questions. Seriously. Extra work is how they get you.

00:00:12.085 --> 00:00:14.830
An equation is a balance.

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:16.790
Whatever you do to one side,

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.370
you do to the other side,

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:19.710
and it stays level.

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:22.450
Okay, look at this one.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.630
Three x plus seven equals twenty-two.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:27.470
And the question says:

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:30.250
what is the value of three x?

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.150
Not x. Three x.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:34.590
So I circle that,

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:36.730
right now, before I do anything else.

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:39.390
Subtract seven from both sides.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.490
Plus seven, minus seven:

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:45.190
gone. Twenty-two minus seven is fifteen.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:47.550
So three x equals fifteen.

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:50.710
And stop. Right there.

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:52.730
Three x is fifteen.

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:54.270
That is the answer.

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:56.910
But a lot of people keep going,

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:58.190
divide by three,

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:00.170
get five, and pick five.

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.430
Which is sitting right there in the choices,

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:03.830
waiting for them.

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:08.770
Your turn. Five y minus four equals twenty-six.

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:10.870
What is five y?

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:12.410
Go on, I'll wait.

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:22.690
Thirty! Add four to both sides,

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:25.010
and stop. If you got thirty,

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:27.730
you're already better at this than you were two minutes

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:28.630
ago.

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:30.890
On multiple choice,

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:32.130
there's another move:

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:33.690
try the answers.

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:37.650
Put a choice into the original equation and see if it balances.

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:39.410
Three times five,

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:41.190
plus seven. Twenty-two.

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:42.730
It works!

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:46.850
But careful. Plugging in found x.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:48.470
X is five.

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:51.010
The question wanted three x.

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:54.970
So don't stop at x when the question asks for three x.

00:01:55.630 --> 00:01:58.670
And whatever you try has to work in the original equation,

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:00.570
not a line you changed along the way.

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:05.350
One habit. Underline what they're asking for,

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.090
before you calculate anything.

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:08.690
Do that every time,

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:11.250
and this trap never gets you.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:12.470
Now hit Try this skill,

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:13.470
and go get 'em!
